Agreement, Lessor shall have the right to terminate this Lease, however Lessor, in order to
declare a default based upon Lessee's failure to pay rental payments required by this Lease or the
Asset Purchase Agreement, shall first send written notice by certified mail or other provable
means of service of such failure by certified mail to Lessee at the address set forth below and
shall permit Lessee fifteen (15) calendar days after Lessee’s receipt of such notice within which
to fully correct and cure such failure.
In order to declare a default based upon Lessee's failure to pay any additional payment or
toperform any other obligation required by this Lease on a timelybasis, Lessor shall have the
right to terminate thislease agreement, however Lessor, in order to declare a default based upon
any such failure, shall first send written notice of such failure by certified mail or other provable
means of service to Lessee at the address set forth below and shall permit Lessee thirty (30)
calendar days after Lessee's receipt of such notice within which to fully correct and cure such
failure.
In the event that Lessee fails to completely cure and correct any such failure within the
time period allowed, Lessee shall be in default and Lessor may, at Lessor's election, provide to
Lessee written notice of termination of this Lease.Upon receipt of such notice, Lessee shall
immediately vacate the premises and returm all keys and Lessor's property in Lessee's possession
to Lessor.Lessee shall remove their or its personal property to Lessor within five (5) days
following Lessor's notice of termination. Any property of Lessee not removed shall be
considered to havebeen abandoned by Lessee.
